# Getting help
> AmigaDOS commands answer a question mark: Dir ?. In vsh, the builtin `help` lists the
> shell's builtins, `man NAME` shows the manual page of a program (paged through less;
> Q leaves it), and many programs print a short summary with `--help`.
> The `tldr NAME` command shows a short page of examples (it fetches the page, so it needs a network),
> and the line `/help` at the vsh prompt lists UP-Term's own settings commands.
? List the shell's builtins with help.
= case "$LEARN_LINE" in help) true ;; *) false ;; esac
~ Type help.
! help
? Read the manual page of ls.
= case "$LEARN_LINE" in "man ls") true ;; *) false ;; esac
~ Type man ls. Press Q to leave the page.
! man ls
? Ask the program cat for its own summary with --help.
= case "$LEARN_LINE" in "cat --help") true ;; *) false ;; esac
~ Type cat --help (two dashes).
! cat --help
